# The mach_timebase_info cache was a single AtomicU64 - the only AtomicU64 use in
# libstd without a target_has_atomic fallback. Split it into two AtomicU32s
# (denom==0 is the uninitialized sentinel; numer is published by the Release store
# of denom) so libstd builds on targets without 64-bit atomics (32-bit PowerPC).
--- library/std/src/sys/unix/time.rs
+++ library/std/src/sys/unix/time.rs
@@ -223,7 +223,7 @@
